    "description": "A British soldier in a netted steel helmet and khaki battledress marches forward under the weight of a heavy pack, a rifle slung over his shoulder and pouches hanging from his webbing, his head bowed to the road ahead. The painterly color treatment keeps the frame in warm, dusty tones — the mottled backdrop, the worn wool of the battledress, and the dark metal of the rifle all holding the same muted afternoon light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame is a portrait of the march itself, when the pack has become the load and the road has become the work.\n\nHe walks, and the road does not hurry him.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
