    "title": "The Stern Look",
    "description": "An older Canadian soldier in a netted steel helmet and khaki battledress looks off to the side with a stern, unsmiling expression, round glasses on his face and a red shoulder patch on his sleeve, a heavy pack on his back. The painterly color treatment keeps the frame in pale, washed-out tones — the netted helmet, the worn wool of the battledress, and the clouded sky behind him all holding the same flat, overcast light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame is a study in a face that has stopped waiting for good news — the glasses, the netting, and the mouth that will not smile.\n\nHe does not look at the camera, and the camera does not look away.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
