    "description": "Two American soldiers walk together across an open field, their rifles slung loose over their shoulders and their packs on their backs, talking as they go. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniforms, the worn leather of the packs, and the pale, hazy field all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the talk between battles, when two men on the same road have nothing to do but walk and remember the place they came from.\n\nThe road goes on, and the talk goes on with it, and the field stays open ahead of them.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
