    "story": "The beret is a promise the Corps made to itself: these ones go first. First onto the beach, first up the cliff, first through the door. The road ahead of them ends in the part of the war that starts hardest, and the whole column walks like men who have already read the ending and signed anyway. They do not look back. Looking back is for men whose war is behind them.",
    "notes": "A column of men with their backs turned is hard to sell and easy to keep. The green berets and the red patches say who they are, the rifles at the shoulder and the packs full of gear say where they are going, and not one of them looks back. Hang it at the end of the longest wall, and let the line of men walk the eye straight off the frame.",
