    "description": "An American soldier in a steel helmet and glasses stands over a fallen comrade lying face down on the ground, his hand wiping the sweat from his brow, barbed wire and wooden stakes filling the ground behind them. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniform, the worn leather of the web belt, and the pale, hazy backdrop all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the moment after the obstacle: the wire still there, the stakes still there, and the man on the ground still there, and nothing left for the standing man to do but wipe his brow.\n\nThe wire stays where it is, and the man stays where he is, and the hand stays on the brow.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
