    "description": "American soldiers charge forward in a wide line across open ground, rifles at the ready with bayonets fixed and packs on their backs, dust rising around them under a hazy sky. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniforms, the dark metal of the rifles, and the pale dust all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the charge itself: the line going forward together, the bayonets pointing the way, and the far side still ahead of them.\n\nThe dust stays thick, and the line stays wide, and the far side stays ahead.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
