    "story": "The wire doesn't stop a man. It slows him — and out here slow is just another word for seen. So the whole war narrows to a few feet of dirt and a question of timing: the gap is there, the gap has always been there, and the only thing being decided is when. His heart is doing the arithmetic his head already finished. Under. Low. Now — but not yet. The move, when it comes, will take two seconds. The choosing of it is taking the whole picture.",
    "notes": "Nobody walks past this frame without ducking a little. The soldier is halfway under the wire with his rifle low and his hand up at his helmet, the strands crossing the frame in front of him, and the sand and the scrub behind him have nothing to hide in. A collector hangs it low, at shoulder height, so the wire runs level with the eye and the duck stays in the room.",
