    "description": "American soldiers disembark from a landing craft onto a beach, gripping the tall poles of the ramp as they come ashore with rifles on their backs, grinning in the grey light. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniforms, and the dark steel of the poles all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the landing as it happens: the poles, the rifles, the grins, and the beach running open in front of them.\n\nThe ramp stays behind them, and the beach stays ahead, and the grins stay on.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
