    "story": "This is the last minute the day is funny. They're off the boat, onto the sand, grinning like men delivered — and they have been, the way a letter is delivered to an address that hasn't read it yet. The beach ahead of them has a whole education waiting and hasn't said a word of it. Whatever they know in an hour, they don't know now. The grin is real. That's what makes it break your heart: it isn't ignorance. It's the last of the before, still warm.",
    "notes": "Buy it for the grins, keep it for what the grins don't know. This is the landing caught in its last innocent minute — men off the ramp, laughing, before the beach has taught them anything — and that irony is a thing a collector can say out loud in any room: the picture is happiest exactly where it's saddest. It also pairs with \"Find cover!\" — the same shore, an hour deeper into the day.",
