    "story": "Pinned is a verb that runs out. Behind the steel, with the fire keeping their heads at the height of the sand, the men have reached the end of what waiting can do — and the laugh in the middle of them is the sound of pressure finding its seam. Somebody is about to say it. Guys. We got to do something. The words are already in the air like a held breath; the doing of it is standing up, all at once, into whatever the beach has been saving. The laugh will go with them. It usually does.",
    "notes": "It's the rare frame whose title the men in it are practically saying out loud — guys, we got to do something — and a collector gets to tell that story standing in front of it: pinned behind the steel, one man laughing, the decision not yet made. The brag is the suspense. Every other action frame in the set shows the doing; this one shows the second before, held indefinitely, and rooms feel it.",
