    "title": "Incoming",
    "description": "An American soldier braces himself behind a steel hedgehog beam on a beach, his mouth open and his hand on the steel, a wire strand crossing the frame in front of him and his pack riding high on his back. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniform, and the dark steel of the beam all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the flinch: the hand on the steel, the mouth open, and the wire drawn across the frame between the man and whatever is coming.\n\nThe beam stays where it is, and the man stays behind it, and the wire stays across the frame.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "A painterly color photograph of an American World War II soldier bracing himself behind a steel hedgehog beam on a beach, his mouth open and his hand on the steel, a wire strand crossing the frame in front of him. Painterly fine art photography, World War II, Facing History.",
