    "description": "An American soldier in a netted steel helmet leans forward as he walks through low scrub, his rifle held across his body and his pack high on his back. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniform, the worn leather of the straps, and the pale, hazy brush all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the walk itself: the lean, the rifle across the body, and the brush coming up around his boots.\n\nThe lean stays forward, and the rifle stays across his body, and the brush stays around his boots.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
