    "story": "The word was for the man behind him. It got as far as his open mouth and died there — because whatever stopped him is still ahead of them in the brush, and a warning spoken is a position given. So the word hangs. His whole body has become the message now: the crouch, the stillness, the face turned back saying it without sound. Go low. Go quiet. The brush ahead has something in it, and it heard them first.",
    "notes": "The whole picture is a word that never gets said. A soldier turned back toward his own line, mouth open, warning swallowed because speaking would give them away — and a collector can tell that story in one breath and watch it land. It is the set's purest suspense frame: nothing has happened yet, and everything is about to. Rooms hold it the way you hold a breath.",
