    "story": "There is a speed where turning back stops being a thing a body can do. He is past it. The shout that left him when the charge started is still leaving — a man at full tilt makes his own weather, noise first, then the bayonet, then the rest of him arriving all at once. Behind him the others are coming the same way, and that's the machinery of it: each man is the reason the man in front can't stop. He isn't running at the enemy so much as being faithfully delivered.",
