    "story": "A running man can't think — his world narrows to the back of the man in front and the ground arriving under his boots. So the thinking gets done by one man for all of them: the one in front, choosing. The cover he's chosen is still just a shape in the distance to everybody behind him, a rumor with a direction. They run on his eyes the way passengers ride on a driver's. If the shape turns out to be nothing, they will be caught in the open still trusting him. He knows the price of being followed. It makes a man choose carefully and run like he didn't.",
    "notes": "This is the set's picture about being led. A line of men at a run, all of them riding on the front man's eyes — and the brag for a collector is that it shows the least photographed thing in any war: trust at speed. Guests read it instantly because everyone has been the man in the middle of that line somewhere in their life. It carries a hallway the way the men carry the pace — without slowing down.",
