    "description": "Two American soldiers take position behind a steel hedgehog on a beach, one firing his rifle over the top of a beam with spent brass casings in the air above him while the other holds his rifle upright and watches the ground ahead. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the sand, the khaki uniforms, and the dark steel of the hedgehog all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the firing over the beam: the rifle up, the brass in the air, and the second man standing by with his rifle upright.\n\nThe beam stays where it is, and the brass stays in the air, and the watching man stays upright.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
