    "id": "i-dLCkS26",
    "title": "On the March",
    "description": "American soldiers march in profile across open ground, a sergeant with three chevrons on his sleeve leading with his rifle in both hands and a heavy pack on his back, other soldiers following in step behind him. The painterly color treatment holds the frame in warm, muted tones — the khaki uniforms, the worn wood of the rifles, and the pale, hazy ground all carrying the same soft light.\n\nPart of a broader body of painterly fine art photography, this World War II frame holds the march: the sergeant in front, the rifles in hand, and the line keeping step behind him.\n\nThe pace stays steady, and the line stays in step, and the ground stays flat under them.\n\n© Wayne Heim",
    "alt": "A painterly color photograph of American World War II soldiers marching in profile across open ground, a sergeant with three chevrons on his sleeve leading with his rifle in both hands, other soldiers following in step behind him. Painterly fine art photography, World War II, Facing History.",
